WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I texted you pretty
much after every episode.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Last Man"
was such a fantastic show.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Five years?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Aww, thanks.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you didn't,
as you wrote --

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought it had
a wonderful ending.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.880 line:92%
I know you did not fully know

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that would be your last
season as you wrote it.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
So then did you have ideas
for other things

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you did not get
a chance to do?

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We knew very fully
how we would handle

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.260
the cliffhanger version
leading off into a fifth season,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.399
but we weren't sure how we would
do the final ending of the show.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were a couple things
along the way,

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:39.039
a couple ideas along the way
of how to ultimately end it.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of them was this idea
of talking --

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the very final segment
of the show

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be me in the offices
at Fox

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.151 size:84% position:42% line:92%
pitching them the show.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then them asking,
"Okay, okay,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:58.358
so we understand all that,
but what is this show about?"

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it would just be me
sitting there

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.064 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for like three minutes

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.999 line:92%
and then then just going,

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"I don't know."

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.836 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And then it would end.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:14.808
And then there was one other,
very weird ending that I wrote.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have it right here.
-Oh, you have it?

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.112 line:92%
-Yeah, I have it right here.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:23.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it would start on a cat
with its eyes closed.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And then you would hear

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:30.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
my voice coming in saying,
"Pebbles? Pebbles.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Pebbles."

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.759 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Then the cats eyes open

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.995 size:84% position:42%
and you would see Tandy
standing over the cat

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would say,
"What's up with you?

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.999 line:92%
You have a little cat dream?"

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.168 line:92%
And then there's no response.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd say, "Do you want to
tell me about it?"

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:50.510
And then Carol, Kristen Schaal's
character, Carol comes in

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
and says "Tandy,
That's so silly.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.482 line:92%
We all know cats can't talk...

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:59.385
unless they have their
vocalization collars on."

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.155 line:92%
So we put a collar on the cat.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.860
Slide it around the cat and then
the cat starts talking.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the cat says,
"I had the craziest dream.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:13.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
You both were in it.
Tandy, you were an idiot."

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.936
And then it goes on to be
this "Wizard of Oz"-type ending

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.371 size:84% position:42%
where every character
from the show comes in.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The whole show
was the cat's dream?

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was the cat's dream.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.844
-People were not crazy about it.
-They were not crazy about it?

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.146 line:92%
-They were not crazy about it.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't know, maybe Fox
caught wind of this

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, canceled the show.
They're like, "We're out.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're fully out."
[ Laughter ]

